<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mhlangana</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1828">1828</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mhlangana was a son of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zulu-kingdom">Zulu</a> chief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senzangakhona">Senzangakhona</a> and a half-brother of Shaka. In September 1828 he and his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dingane">Dingane</a> assassinated Shaka at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dukuza">Dukuza</a>. Soon afterwards Dingane, fearing his ambitions, had Mhlangana killed and took the Zulu throne alone, ruling until 1840.</p></div>
